<header><p class="enc-kicker">People / group</p><h1 class="enc-title">House of Hauteville</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">11th–12th century</span> · <a href="/centuries/11th-century">11th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The House of Hauteville was a Norman family from Hauteville-la-Guichard in the Cotentin whose sons won lands in southern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/italy">Italy</a> from the 1030s. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/robert-guiscard">Robert Guiscard</a> became duke of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/apulia">Apulia</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/calabria">Calabria</a>, his brother Roger I conquered <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sicily">Sicily</a> between 1061 and 1091, and Roger II united these lands as the Kingdom of Sicily in 1130. Bohemond founded the Principality of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/antioch">Antioch</a>, and the family ruled Sicily until 1194.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/house-of-hauteville.jpg" alt="House of Hauteville" width="320" height="366" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: The White Lion · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Coat_of_Arms_of_the_House_of_Hauteville_(according_to_Agostino_Inveges).svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
